# SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-only
#
# The automap comes back after the reader's full screen on Curse of the
# Azure Bonds, and Tab is still its key (#588; rdr-map-back.leg and #332
# are Pool of Radiance's). The reader's give-back asks the program to
# compose the adventuring screen, whose roster is drawn over the
# automap's own cells; on this program the composer and the roster's
# drawer are overlaid and called through stub entries (`docs/seams.md`
# §10), so the path differs and the claim is the same: the map up before
# the log is the map up after it. `tests/sessions/curse-map-reader.rec`
# is the same walk as hashes.
# A single leg: `N` reaches the program in a seam-off run, and Tab is
# the automap's, so a seam-off run has no map to compare against.
# Driven on the Steam copy with its shipped slots (`curse-slots`).

about the automap comes back after the journal's full screen on Curse, and Tab still works
kind single
program START.EXE
speed 386
store tests/visual/curse-reader-store.txt
seam automap
seam journal
until 151133600
every 25

key P@2500
key A@2650
key Return@2800
key L@2950
key A@3100
key B@3250
key Return@3550
key Return@3850
key Left@4000
key Left@4600
key Up@4750
key Return@4900
key Return@5050

# Tab for the map, `Notes` for the log, Return for entry 31 and `NEXT`
# for its second page; `EXIT` twice. Then Tab twice: the first takes the
# map away and the second brings it back.
key Tab@5200
key N@5350
key Return@5500
key N@5800
key E@6400
key E@6700
key Tab@7000
key Tab@7300

# The roster, before the map; the map over it; the log, the two pages
# and the log again over the whole screen.
same 5100-5200
same 5225-5350
same 5375-5500
same 5525-5800
same 5825-6400
same 6425-6700

# The map back, and holding still.
same 6725-7000

# The whole claim, as two frames: the screen with the map on it before
# `Notes`, and the screen after the second `EXIT`. Every pixel, the bar
# row included.
equal 5225 6725

# And the key was not spent: Tab puts the roster back as it was before
# the first Tab, and Tab again puts the map back as it was.
same 7025-7300
equal 5175 7025
same 7325-7575
equal 5225 7325
